  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="3">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:WlArt">Wl art</ref> 3</head>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="la" source="#robertson" n="3" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="238" ed="#robertson"/>Volo autem, ut omnes homines quos mecum adduxi aut post me venerunt sint in pace mea et quiete.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="239" ed="#robertson"/>I desire likewise that all the men whom I brought with me or who have come after me shall enjoy the benefit of my protection.</ab>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:WlArtRetr_3">Wl art retr 3</ref>; <ref target="clause:LeisWl_22">Leis Wl 22</ref></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="409"><ref target="clause:LeisWl_22">Leis Wl 22</ref></note>
        <note type="editorial">Added October 2026 from Robertson pp. 238–239 (text and translation); Liebermann’s text (K–M) not yet added</note>
      </div>
